.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAM-LIST-ACCOUNTS 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eam-list-accounts \- list Euclid accounts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B eam list-accounts
[\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fIPREFIX\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-size\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-index\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-sort\-column\fR \fICOLUMN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists accounts via the eam service's
.I list-accounts
action. The caller must be authenticated as a global administrator (see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1)).
.PP
The JSON response, containing the matching accounts and the total account
count, is printed to standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-prefix " " \fIPREFIX\fR
Only return accounts whose account ID starts with \fIPREFIX\fR. If
omitted, all accounts match.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-page\-size " " \fIN\fR
Maximum number of accounts to return. \fI0\fR or less (the default,
\fI\-1\fR) means no limit.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-page\-index " " \fIN\fR
Zero-based page index, applied when \fB\-\-page\-size\fR is set. Defaults to
\fI\-1\fR (meaningless while paging is off).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-sort\-column " " \fICOLUMN\fR
Field to sort by: \fIaccountId\fR (default) or \fIname\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The listing was retrieved.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, the request could not be sent, or the caller is not an
authenticated global administrator. If the failure was an expired or
invalid session (\fIHTTP 401\fR), the stored credentials file is removed;
run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again before retrying.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam list-accounts
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-account (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-delete-account (1)
